def consumer(q):
    while True:
        process(q.get())
        time.sleep(10)

output:
**Issue:** Bounded queue filled while the producer blocks and no consumer slot frees up.
**Why:** If the consumer itself waits on the producer (e.g. joins it) you get a circular wait deadlock; even alone, put() has no timeout so shutdown hangs.
**Fix:**
def producer(q):
    for item in items:
        try:
            q.put(item, timeout=5)
        except queue.Full:
            logger.warning('dropping %r', item)
            break

